keywords:
  - semiconductor
  - visualization
  - process flow
  - materials
  - Python
abstract: >-
  A Python package for drawing semiconductor structures and expressing simple
  fabrication flows. A structure is authored once as a process, then drawn by
  whichever of three renderers preserves it: a vector isometric engine, a 2D
  cross-section renderer, or a true-solid Boolean backend built on trimesh,
  manifold3d and PyVista. One material palette runs through all three, where
  hue gives the chemical family and lightness tracks electron density, so
  related figures agree with one another. Every text size is points at print
  width and no renderer accepts anything below 7 pt. A model can be saved as
  a JSON process document and replayed to the same geometry, and the same
  operations are available from a command line and over the Model Context
  Protocol.
